"hadiths[66]{hadithnumber,text}:"
1080,"Abu Ayyub narrated that :The Messenger of Allah said: ""Four are from the Sunan of the Messengers: Al-Hayat"
1081,"Abdullah bin Mas'ud narrated:""We went with Allah's Messenger, while we were young men who had nothing. He said: 'O young men! You should marry, for indeed it helps in lowering the gaze and protecting the private parts. Whoever among you is not able to marry, then let him fast, for indeed fasting will diminish his sexual desire."""
1082,"Sa'eed bin Al-Musayyab narrated from Sa'b bin Abi Waqqas:""The Messenger of Allah refused Uthman bin Ma'zun (when he asked) regarding celibacy"
1083,"Abu Hurairah narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said: ""When someone whose religion and character you are pleased with proposes to (someone under the care) of one of you"
1084,"Abu Hatim Al-Muzani narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said: ""When someone whose religion and character you are pleased with comes to you then marry (her to) him. If you do not do so"
1085,"Jabir narrated that:The Prophet said: ""Indeed the woman is married for her religion"
1086,Bakr bin Abdullah Al-Muzani narrated that :Al-Mughirah bin Shu'bah proposed to a woman
1087,"Abu Al-Balj narrated from Muhammad bin Hatib Al-Jumahi who said that:The Messenger of Allah said: ""The distinction between the lawful and the unlawful is the Duff and the voice"
1088,"Aishah narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said: ""Publicize this marriage"
1089,"Ar-Rubai bint Muawwidh said:""The morning after the consummation of my marriage"
1090,Abu Hurairah narrated that:When supplicating for the newlywed
1091,"Ibn Abbas narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said: ""If anyone of you"
1092,"Aishah narrated:""The Messenger of Allah married me in Shawwal"
1093,Anas bin Malik narrated:The Messenger of Allah saw some traces of saffron on `Abdur-Rahman bin `Awf so he said: 'What is this?' He said: 'I married a woman for the amount of gold equal to a date stone.' So he said: 'May Allah bless you. Have a banquet
1094,"Anas bin Malik narrated:""The Prophet had a banquet for Safiyyah bint Huyayy with Sawiq and dates"
1095,(Another chain similar to the narration as no. 1095) :Others have reported this Hadith from Ibn Uyainah
1096,"Ibn Mas'ud narrated that :The Messenger of Allah said: ""Having food on the first day is was is obligatory"
1097,"Ibn Umar narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said: ""Accept the invitation when you are offered"
1098,"Abu Mas'ud narrated:""A man named Abu Shu'aib came to a slave of his"
1099,"Jabir bin Abdullah narrated:""I married a woman and went to the Prophet"
1100,"Abu Musa narrated that :the Messenger of Allah said: ""There is no marriage except with a Wali"
1101,"Aishah narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said: ""Whichever woman married without the permission of her Wali her marriage is invalid"
1102,"Ibn Abbas narrated that :the Prophet said: ""The adulteresses are the ones who marry themselves without Bayyinah (proof)"
1103,"Narrated by Ali ibn Hujr, who reported from Sharik ibn Abdullah, from Abu Ishaq — and also narrated by Qutaybah, who reported from Abu Awana, from Abu Ishaq — and also narrated by Muhammad ibn Bashshar, who reported from Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi, from Isra'il, from Abu Ishaq — and also narrated by Abdullah ibn Abi Ziyad, who reported from Zayd ibn Hubab, from Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him), who said:

The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: **""There is no marriage without a guardian (wali).""**

It is also narrated in this chapter from Aisha, Ibn Abbas, Abu Hurayrah, Imran ibn Husayn, and Anas (may Allah be pleased with them all)."
1104,
1105,"Abu Hurairah narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said: ""Every Khutbah that does not have the Tashah-hud in it"
1106,"Abu Hurairah narrated that:The Prophet said: ""A matron should not be given in marriage until she is consulted"
1107,"Ibn Abbas narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said: ""The matron has more right to herself than her Wali"
1108,"Abu Hurairah narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said: ""An orphan is to be consulted about herself"
1109,"Samurah bin Jundab narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said: ""Whichever woman is given in marriage by two Wali"
1110,"Jabir bin Abdullah narrated that:The Prophet said: ""Whichever slave gets married without the permission of his owner"
1111,"(Another chain) Jabir bin Abdullah narrated that:Abdullah narrated that the Prophet said: ""Whichever slave gets married without the permission of his owner"
1112,"Abdullah bin Amr bin Rabi'ah narrated from his father:""A woman from Banu Fazarah was married for (the dowry of) two sandals. So the Messenger of Allah said to her: 'Do you approve of (exchanging) yourself and your wealth for two sandals?' She said: 'Yes.'"" He said: ""So he permitted it"
1113,"Sahl bin Sa'd As-Sa'idi narrated that:A woman came to the Messenger of Allah and said: ""I present myself to you (for marriage)."" So she stood for a long time. Then a man said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Marry her to me if you have no need of her."" So he said: ""Do you have anything to give her as a dowry?"" He said: ""I have nothing except this Izar."" So the Messenger of Allah said: ""If you give her your Izar then you will have no Izar"
1114,"Abu Ayyub narrated that :The Messenger of Allah said: ""Four are from the Sunan of the Messengers: Al-Hayat"
1115,"Abu Burdah bin Abi Musa narrated from his father that the Messenger of Allah said:""Three will receive their reward twice: A slave who fulfills the rights of Allah and the rights of his owners"
1116,"# Hadith of Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi (may Allah be pleased with him)

**Narrated by al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Khallal, who narrated to us: Ishaq ibn 'Isa and 'Abdullah ibn Nafi' al-Sa'igh, who both said: Malik ibn Anas informed us, from Abu Hazim ibn Dinar, from Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi (may Allah be pleased with him), that:**

A woman came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, ""I have offered myself to you."" She stood for a long while. Then a man said, ""O Messenger of Allah, marry her to me if you have no need for her."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, **""Do you have anything that you could give her as a dowry (sadaq)?""** He replied, ""I have nothing but this izar (lower garment) of mine."" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, **""If you give her your izar, you will sit without an izar. Seek something else.""** He said, ""I cannot find anything."" He ﷺ said, **""Seek something, even if it be a ring of iron.""** He sought but found nothing. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, **""Do you have any portion of the Qur'an with you?""** He replied, ""Yes, such-and-such a surah and such-and-such a surah"" — naming certain surahs. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, **""I have married her to you with what you have of the Qur'an.""**

---

**Abu 'Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said:** This is a *hasan sahih* hadith.

**Imam al-Shafi'i** (may Allah have mercy upon him) acted upon this hadith, stating: If a man has nothing to give as a dowry and marries a woman upon a surah of the Qur'an, the marriage is valid, and he should teach her a surah of the Qur'an.

**Some of the scholars of knowledge** said: The marriage is valid, and he should give her a dowry equivalent to her *mahr al-mithl* (customary dowry of her like). This is the position of the people of Kufah, **Ahmad**, and **Ishaq**.

---

*Related: Sahih al-Bukhari, Sahih Muslim, Sunan al-Tirmidhi, Kitab al-Nikah.*"
1117,"Aishah narrated:""The wife of Rifa'ah Al-Qurzi came to the Messenger of Allah and said: 'I was with Rifa'ah and he divorced me irrevocably. Then I married Abdur-Rahman bin Az-Zubair"
1118,"Jabir bin Abdullah and Ali narrated:""The Messenger of Allah cursed the Muhill and the one the Muhallal was done for"
1119,"Abdullah bin Mas'ud narrated:""The Messenger of Allah cursed the Muhill and the one the Muhallal was done for"
1120,"Ali bin Abi Talib narrated:""The Prophet prohibited the Mut'ah with women"
1121,"Muhammad bin Ka'b narrated that:Ibn Abbas said: ""Mut'ah was only during the beginning of Islam. A man would arrive in a land that he was not familiar with so he would marry a woman for the extent of time that he thought he would remain there. So his Mut'ah was upheld and his case was fine until the (following) Ayah was revealed: Except their wives or what their right hands possess. Then every private part other than those became unlawful"
1122,"Imran bin Husain narrated that :The Prophet said: ""There is no Jalab"
1123,"# Translation of the Hadith

**Narrated by 'Abdullāh ibn Mas'ūd (may Allāh be pleased with him):**

He said: ""The Messenger of Allāh (peace and blessings be upon him) cursed the one who performs a marriage solely for the purpose of making a woman lawful (*al-muḥill*) and the one for whom she is made lawful (*al-muḥallal lahu*).""

Abū 'Īsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: ""This is a *ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ* hadith. And Abū Qays al-Awdī's name is 'Abd al-Raḥmān ibn Tharwān. This hadith has been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) through other chains of narration. The practice (*al-'amal*) according to the people of knowledge among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) — including 'Umar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, 'Uthmān ibn 'Affān, 'Abdullāh ibn 'Umar, and others — is based upon this hadith. It is also the position of the jurists among the *Tābi'ūn*, and it is the view held by Sufyān al-Thawrī, Ibn al-Mubārak, al-Shāfi'ī, Aḥmad, and Isḥāq.""

He further said: ""I heard al-Jārūd ibn Mu'adh narrate from Wakī' that he held this view and said: 'The proponents of *ra'y* (personal opinion) should be condemned for their stance on this issue.' Al-Jārūd said: Wakī' also reported that Sufyān (al-Thawrī) said: 'If a man marries a woman solely to make her lawful for her former husband, and then it occurs to him to keep her, it is not permissible for him to retain her unless he marries her with a fresh, new marriage contract (*nikāḥ jadīd*).'""

---

**Note:** This hadith addresses the prohibition of *taḥlīl* marriage — a marriage contracted with the premeditated intention of divorcing the woman so that she may lawfully return to her former husband after a triple divorce (*ṭalāq*). Both the man who enters such a contract (*muḥill*) and the former husband who arranges it (*muḥallal lahu*) are subject to the curse (*la'nah*) of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)."
1124,"Ibn Abbas narrated:""The Prophet prohibited marrying a woman along with her paternal aunt or along with her maternal aunt"
1125,"Abu Hurairah narrated:""The Messenger of Allah prohibited that a woman be married along with her paternal aunt"
1126,"Uqbah bin Amir Al-Juhani narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said: ""Indeed the conditions most deserving to be fulfilled are those that make the private parts lawful among you"
1127,"Ibn Umar narrated:""Ghilan bin Salamah Ath-Thaqafi accepted Islam and he had ten wives in Jahiliyyah who accepted Islam along with him. So the Prophet ordered (him) to chose four (of them)"
1128,"Abu Wahb Al-Jaishani narrated that:He heard Ibn Fairuz Ad-Dhailami narrating from his father: ""I went to the Prophet and said: 'O Messenger of Allah! I accepted Islam and I had two sisters (as wives).' So the Messenger of Allah said: 'Chose whichever of them you will"
1129,"Abu Wahb Al-Jaishani narrated from Ad-Dhahhak bin Fairuz Ad-Dailami from his father:""I said: 'O Messenger of Allah! I accepted Islam and I had two sisters (as wives).' So Messenger of Allah said: 'Chose whichever of them you will"
1130,"Ruwaifi bin Thabit narrated that :the Prophet said: ""Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day"
1131,"Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri narrated:""We got some captives on the day of Awtas"
1132,"Abu Mas'ud Al-Ansari narrated:""The Messenger of Allah prohibited the price of a dog"
1133,"Abu Hurairah narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said: ""A man is not to sell over his brother's sale"
1134,"Abu Bakr bin Al-Jahm narrated:""Abu Salamah bin Abdur-Rahman and I visited Fatimah bint Qais. She narrated to us that her husband had divorced her three times"
1135,"Jabir narrated:""We said: 'O Messenger of Allah! We practice Azl"
1136,"Jabir bin Abdullah narrated:""We practiced Azl while the Qur'an was being revealed"
1137,"Abu Sa'eed narrated:""Azl was mentined before the Messenger of Allah and he said: 'Why would one of you do that?"
1138,"# Translation of the Hadith

**Narrated by Mahmūd ibn Ghaylān**, who said: **Abū Dāwūd** narrated to us, who said: **Shuʿbah** informed us, who said: **Abū Bakr ibn Abī al-Jahm** informed me, who said:

I and **Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān** entered upon **Fāṭimah bint Qays**, and she narrated to us that her husband had divorced her with a triple *ṭalāq* (irrevocable divorce) and had not assigned for her any lodging (*suknā*) nor maintenance (*nafaqah*).

She said: ""And he placed with a paternal cousin of his ten *aqfizah* for me — five of barley and five of wheat.""

She said: ""So I came to the **Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him**, and I mentioned that to him.""

She said: ""So he said: **'He has spoken the truth.'**""

She said: ""Then he commanded me to observe my *ʿiddah* (waiting period) in the house of **Umm Sharīk**. Then the **Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him**, said to me: **'Indeed, the house of Umm Sharīk is a house frequented by the Muhājirūn (Emigrants). Rather, observe your ʿiddah in the house of Ibn Umm Maktūm, for perhaps you may cast aside your garments and he will not see you. And when your ʿiddah has expired and someone comes seeking your hand in marriage, then inform me.'**""

She said: ""When my ʿiddah had expired, **Abū Jahm** and **Muʿāwiyah** proposed to me.""

She said: ""So I came to the **Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him**, and I mentioned that to him. He said: **'As for Muʿāwiyah, he is a man who possesses no wealth; and as for Abū Jahm, he is a man who is harsh with women.'**""

She said: ""Then **Usāmah ibn Zayd** proposed to me, and I married him. And **Allah blessed me through Usāmah.**""

---

**This is a *ṣaḥīḥ* (authentic) hadith.**

It was also narrated by **Sufyān al-Thawrī** from **Abū Bakr ibn Abī al-Jahm**, in a narration similar to this hadith, and he added therein that the **Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him**, said to her: **""Marry Usāmah.""**

**Narrated by Mahmūd ibn Ghaylān**, who said: **Wakīʿ** narrated to us from **Sufyān**, from **Abū Bakr ibn Abī al-Jahm**, with this (chain and text)."
1139,"Aishah narrated that:The Prophet would divide (his time) equally between his wives and said: ""O Allah! This is my division in what I have control over"
1140,"Abu Hurairah narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said: ""When a man has two wives and he is not just between them"
1141,"Narrated to us by Ibn Abi 'Umar and Qutaybah, who both said: narrated to us Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Qaz'ah ibn Yahya, from Abu Sa'id (may Allah be pleased with him), who said:

The practice of *'azl* (coitus interruptus) was mentioned in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and he said: **""Why would one of you do that?""**

Ibn Abi 'Umar added in his narration: **""Let none of you do that.""**

Both narrators stated in their version: **""Indeed, there is no soul that is created, except that Allah is its Creator.""**

He (the narrator) said: In this chapter, there is also a narration from Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him).

Abu 'Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said: The hadith of Abu Sa'id is a *hasan sahith* (good and authentic) hadith. It has been narrated through multiple chains from Abu Sa'id (may Allah be pleased with him). A group of scholars among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and others considered *'azl* to be disliked (*makruh*)."
1142,"Ibn Abbas narrated:""The Prophet returned his daughter Zainab to Abul-As bin Ar-Rabi after six years in the first marriage without renewing the marriage"
1143,"Ibn Abbas narrated:""A man became a Muslim during the time of the Prophet"
1144,Alqamah narrated that :Ibn Mas'ud was asked about a man who married a woman and he did not stipulate the dowry for her
1145,Ali (bin Abi Talib) narrated that The Messenger of Allah said:“Indeed Allah has made unlawful through suckling whatever He made unlawful through lineage.”
